... but what about the other way around?  If I can apply my stethescope
once per turn for free, the only time this patch affects anything is if
there're multiple monsters next to me and there are two or more that
are damaged - kind of odd since the normal strategy is whack one 'till
it's dead - and it's somehow important to know the health of the
monster I just whacked (mostly if I'm surrounded it tends to be because
of a summoning storm, and I can see checking the summoner being
important but I'm not so sure about the benefit of having some
intentionally vague idea of the health of the creature I just hit...

I think this patch is mostly irrelevant.  If you get multiple strong
monsters next to you and you're dealing damage to all of them (not
smart anyway) it could help a very little bit, but mostly all it does
is save you the trouble of using your stethescope on the monster every
turn.

Interesting idea anyway... maybe this could be given instead of a
stethescope?  That seems a little extreme, but... I don't know.
There's probably some way it could be used without being trivial...

